course: dictionary
lesson: 8818
title: Many meanings of shell
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A shell is a hard outer cover that protects something soft inside. «Zoe found 12 shells on the beach.» Shells are things you can count, like pebbles or coins.
explain: The same word can mean different things, so use the context to decide. «The jaguar can crack turtle shells» means the hard covers of turtles. «The chick cracks the shell» means the hard outside of an egg. «A cast is a hard shell of plaster» means a hard outer case, not an animal at all.
explain: Shell can also be a verb. «Shelling peas» means taking the peas out of their shells. Ask yourself: what word would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence to check it still makes sense.
fact: A shell is the hard outer cover of an animal such as a snail, clam, crab or turtle.
fact: «Shell» can also mean the hard outside of an egg or a nut.
fact: «Shell» can mean any hard outer case, like the shell of a building.
fact: To shell something means to take it out of its shell, as in «shelling peas».
fact: Long ago, «cowrie shells» were used as money in parts of Africa and Asia.
exercise: «Zoe found 12 shells on the beach.» How many shells did Zoe find? | 1 | 21 | 4 | *12
exercise: «The chick cracks the shell with a hard tip on its beak.» What is the shell here? | A sea animal's home | A nut's soft middle | A kind of plaster | *The hard outer cover of an egg
exercise: «Shelling peas» means | Growing peas in a garden | *Taking peas out of their shells | Counting peas in a bag | Cooking peas in a pan
test: «A cast is a hard shell of plaster that stops a broken bone moving.» In this sentence, shell means | A nut's hard cover | A thing you find on a beach | A sea animal's cover | *A hard outer case
test: Which word fits best? «The jaguar can crack turtle ___ and caiman skulls.» | *Shells | Ropes | Leaves | Sails
exam: «Cashews are sold shelled and cooked.» What does shelled mean here? | Cooked in a pan | *With their hard outer cases taken off | Hatched from an egg | Covered in plaster
